# GitHub OTA release (Kamaz-Leveler)

Firmware checks: `https://api.github.com/repos/timurufa86/kamaz_leveler/releases/latest`

## Required release assets (exact names)

1. `kamaz_leveler.bin` — application firmware (ESP32 app image, same as `*.ino.bin`)
2. `kamaz_leveler.bin.sha256` — hex SHA-256 of that bin (64 chars, typically one line)

## On every version that should be available via OTA

1. Bump SemVer per `semantic-versioning` rule (`8_5_7` ↔ `8.5.7`).
2. Build firmware; copy app bin to `ota_release_X_Y_Z/kamaz_leveler.bin`.
3. Write matching `kamaz_leveler.bin.sha256`.
4. Create/update GitHub Release on `timurufa86/kamaz_leveler`:
   - Tag: `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` (e.g. `v8.5.7`) — must be the **latest** release for devices to see it
   - Upload both assets with the exact names above
5. Confirm with `gh release view <tag> -R timurufa86/kamaz_leveler` that both assets exist.

## Do not

- Upload only the `.bin` without `.sha256` (device rejects incomplete releases).
- Rename assets (code looks up fixed names).
- Leave a newer draft/prerelease as "latest" if devices should not install it yet.
